## Decision honesty
**FIXED path-A for CRIT 7.2 (`c_sys_exec_last_arg`):**

Last-arg extract is defined in `ooda/oodac/c_emit_args.oo` (240 lines).
C-arg text is walked with `char_at` for quote / escape / paren-depth /
top-level comma classification only, then **one**
`str_slice(args, last_start, n)` for the last span. There is no
`out = out + c` / per-char OoStr concat in the last-arg function.
`.oo` has no C `char buf[N]`; the alpha honesty for the SPRINT
“stack buffer” wording is **slice-once-per-span** (same close as
`t1_memory.oot` M-SG3 and 7.1).

Live prove: `scripts/s72_sys_exec_last_arg_smoke.oo` **ALL OK**
(fail-closed SECRET last IDENT; quoted last arg with commas +
SECRET-spelling no-FP). T1/T2 secret smokes that exercise sys_exec
argv remain exit 0. 7.1 scan smoke remains exit 0.

**Still not claimed (do not greenwash):**

| Residual | Status |
|----------|--------|
| **7.10** `c_parse_secret_env` `name = name + c` | open — other OWN |
| **8.6** `c_args_strip_cr` `out = out + c` | same monofile L188+; **not** last-arg |
| `char_at` 1-byte `OoStr` temps while walking | language floor — not quadratic last-arg leak |
| Seed `bootstrap/seed/oodac` still concats | seed is **not** 7.2 proof (`s72_runtime.oot`) |
| Full IFC / `#[Secret]` / interp `${}` | residual (named in harness + ideas) |
| Mid-argv IDENT vs last-span | last-arg is a **comma span**; mid-argv is T2 token walk (`secret_sys_exec_argv_*`) |
| `ci_product.oo` does not wire s72 (or s71) | hygiene residual — T1/T2 only |
| Formal peer / security / memory / hygiene `.oot` still mid-land | ok — smoke + domain + integration + runtime hold close |

Path-A 7.2 ≠ C stack buffer rewrite.
Cap preferred style: smoke green + named residual = FIXED path-A.
**ALREADY_FIXED** path-A: source already sliced; this close is prove + board flip.

